# In the generic version the sum of two values that failed the test for a string may be a number, so it is stored into the string field behind the allocation, by a store that tests it.
# Until then the empty string stands in for it. So the allocation still lists every field, in its order, and `count`, which only the allocation fills and flow calls stored at most once, stays in it.
# Without something to stand in, every field listed from `name` on would have to be defined behind the allocation, which `count` may not be.
# FORM: AsRead
# Hot, because a cold function stays one function: it is not split into tests, a typed body and a fallback.
# OPTIONS: heat=EverythingIsHot
# RUN: pipeline AddGenericVersion
# CHECK: layout L0 name="Named" {{*}}{key="count" {{*}}stores=AtMostOnce
# CHECK: function {{*}} name="make" {{*}}role=GenericVersion
# CHECK: [[sum]]: number|string|bigint ~ string = Add
# CHECK: [[one]]: 1 = Integer integer=1
# CHECK-NEXT: [[filler]]: "" = String string=""
# CHECK-NEXT: [[object]]: L0 = NewObject -, [[filler]], [[one]] layout=L0 fields=[0, 1]
# CHECK-NEXT: PropSet [[object]], [[sum]] key="name"

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
layout L0 name="Named" fields=[{key="name" declared={type=string} flags=[IsRequired]}, {key="count" declared={type=number} flags=[IsRequired]}]

function f0 name="main" kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="input" [isFreeName]
    v2 = CallDirect v1 function=f1
    v3 = PropGet v2 key="name"
    v4 = PropGet v2 key="count"
    v5 = NewArray v3, v4 contents=anything
    Return v5
}
function f1 name="make" parameters=[{type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: anything):
    v1 = Convert v0 declared={type=string} illTypedCause=Assertion
    v2 = Add v1, v1
    v3 = Convert v2 declared={type=string}
    v4 = Integer integer=1
    v5 = Convert v4 declared={type=number}
    v6 = NewObject -, v3, v5 layout=L0 fields=[0, 1]
    v7 = FinishObject v6
    Return v7
}
